 "recommendations": "1. Thor and any Asgardian: mark overstated. Plot the main marker at the human-tissue-equivalent mass, 290.3/3 = 96.8 kg (213 lb). That gives S about 20-22 and plain FFMI about 22-25 at 0-10% fat. Show the as-listed point (S about 57-67) as a faint ghost, joined by a line. Label: \"Official handbooks: Asgardian flesh and bone is about three times as dense as human tissue\". Note that DK's wording names only skin and bones, which would mean a smaller correction. Say \"about\": the factor is a round handbook number.\n\n2. Wolverine: score him at 195 lb (88.5 kg): S about 33-39, FFMI about 29-35 at 0-15% fat. Note that Marvel.com says adamantium \"adds an extra 105 pounds\" (47.6 kg). The 300 lb figure would overstate his score 1.54 times.\n\n3. Colossus: chart his human form (6 ft 6 in, 250 lb; S about 24 at 10% fat) as comparable. Show the armoured form as not comparable: greyed or off-scale, with no score. Officially his body becomes a steel-like substance \"analogous to osmium and to carbon steel\", and its extra mass comes \"from an unknown, perhaps extradimensional source\". The stated 500 lb also cannot be steel at that size (existing key colossus_density_check).\n\n4. The Thing and Luke Cage: plot their listed values with an \"overstated, amount unknown\" mark, such as a hatched or open marker with an arrow pointing down. The Thing's official hide is rock-like. Cage's official tissue is \"very dense muscle and bone\". Do not invent a correction.\n\n5. Hulk (savage, grey, merged) and Abomination: comparable. The official handbook says the added mass is \"bone marrow and tissue\" (Hulk) or \"bone marrow and muscle tissue\" (Abomination). Caveat: \"fortified cellular structure\", with no density factor given. Keep the grey Hulk's stats labelled fan-reported, as builds.json already does.\n\n6. Juggernaut: comparable, with a caveat note: mystical; his helmet and armour may be in the 900 lb, but no source says so.\n\n7. Darkseid and Doomsday: comparable by default, labelled \"no official information on what the mass is made of\". Fan-wiki density claims are shown only as reported.\n\n8. Kingpin: comparable. Quote the official \"bulk does not consist of fat\". Show the fat range down to about 2% (the fan-wiki-only 9 lb), labelled reported, and note that this is below lean contest bodybuilders. Bane, Superman, Black Panther, Captain America and Batman: comparable, using the existing weights; Bane at 350 lb, with 425 lb (Venom) as a variant.\n\n9. On the page, say plainly that no Marvel or DC source gives any character's body-fat percentage. All comic scores therefore use assumed fat and are estimates.\n\n10. In each comic tooltip, give the official composition quote and its status (official or reported), with its source, so readers can see why a point was moved or flagged.",
 "gaps": "1. Partial handbook text only. The OHOTMU volumes on archive.org are lending-library scans. I could read only the full-text search snippets (about 100 OCR characters each), and the search-inside page (inside.php) returned 403. So:\n   - issue numbers and pages are unconfirmed (for example, the Asgardians group entry is probably Deluxe #1);\n   - some sentences are joined from overlapping snippets, and their opening words are missing in places (Colossus's \"The means by which\").\n\n2. Entries I could not see at all:\n   - the OHOTMU Thing, Wolverine, Luke Cage and individual Thor entries;\n   - OHOTMU: Daredevil 2004 (the source of the fan-wiki Kingpin \"9 pounds of fat\");\n   - OHOTMU Master Edition #9 (the fan-wiki Black Panther \"denser tissue\");\n   - Thor & Hercules: Encyclopaedia Mythologica 2009;\n   - the OHOTMU A to Z (2008-10) volumes for these characters.\n\n3. Numbers no source gives:\n   - Wolverine's adamantium mass appears only on Marvel.com (105 lb / 47.6 kg); no handbook figure turned up, and \"nearly 100 pounds\" is fan-wiki text;\n   - no source states a tissue density in kg/m3, the Thing's hide mass, the mass of Juggernaut's helmet or armour, or the mass of Doomsday's bone spurs.\n\n4. DC sources: DC's own Who's Who (1985-87, 1990-92) was not found. DC coverage rests on two DK books plus fan wikis.\n\n5. Marvel.com access: WebFetch returned 403 for Marvel.com. The pages were fetched with curl and a browser user agent on 2026-10-11 (raw copies in scratchpad/research/comic-composition/raw/).\n\n6. Not used as sources: archive.org also holds unauthorised digital comic uploads (for example the Marvel Masterworks Thor digital upload and the \"Kileko-Empire\" collections) that repeat the handbook wording; I deliberately did not cite them.\n\n7. Unresolved Thor ambiguity: OHOTMU says \"flesh and bone\" (whole body) and DK says \"skin and bones\". If only skin and bone are denser, the correction is smaller. That case was not computed, because it needs tissue mass fractions that were outside this topic.\n\n8. Existing keys relied on, not re-researched (heights, weights and existing notes): thor, wolverine, colossus, colossus_density_check, kingpin, bane, juggernaut, hulk_savage, hulk_grey_joe_fixit, hulk_merged_marvelcom, abomination, luke_cage, captain_america, black_panther, batman, superman, darkseid, doomsday, dc_com_no_stats, plausibility_metrics, bauer2023_bodyfat_ranges_review."
